A||||4||kempo||Please pray for the people of the DC area||||1||
Z||000000||kempo||09-11-2001||01:12 PM||||This morning, started as a normal day.  But when I got to school, half hour into it, they started a lockdown.  Right beforehand, I left school.  Almost all schools surrounding the DC area have issued a lockdown and nobody is allowed to go anywhere.  <P>I am asking for your prayers as I have family and friends that work in Downtown Washington, DC, as well as those who have been injured or attacked in the other cities and states.  While on the cellular phone with my father, there were bombs that were going off in the background.  He is safe, but they have closed down all roads and highways in and around the DC area.  This is a very hellish situation, and I am asking for your prayers.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||09-11-2001||05:46 PM||||trade ya prayers. my brother works in washington (not the pentagon, but we're concerned anyway) and we're waiting to hear from him.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieronv||09-11-2001||05:54 PM||||I think the prayers of the entire nation are going to the victims and families of Washington and New York.<P>God Bless you all<BR>Don||||reg||9
Z||000003||Philphine||09-11-2001||06:57 PM||||talked to my sister. he's home. he lives in balto. md. and got caught in the commute confusion. hope anybody else worrying gets good news. i'll hold up my end on the prayers.||||reg||1
